{"role":"assistant","content":"All three fixes are in. Now I'll verify end-to-end against a **local mock** of the Intervals.icu API (using the `INTERVALS_BASE` override — nothing external gets touched). The mock mirrors the documented provider behavior: strict scope validation, token responses without `refresh_token`/`expires_in`.","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"tool_G3I07MgIyCSFjFd8QX9rXPVU","function":{"name":"Write","arguments":"{\"content\":\"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Local mock of the Intervals.icu API, built from the public docs/forum guide.\\n\\nBehavior mirrored:\\n- /oauth/authorize: 400 invalid_request unless every scope is <FAMILY>:READ|WRITE\\n  with FAMILY in the documented set and each family specified at most once\\n  (\\\"For each scope specify READ or WRITE\\\"). On success 302s back with\\n  code + state.\\n- /api/oauth/token: returns token WITHOUT refresh_token and WITHOUT expires_in\\n  (the documented shape).\\n- /api/v1/athlete/<id>/wellness: 200 with data, or 401 after `touch 401` file.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport json, os, sys, time, urllib.parse\\nfrom http.server import BaseHTTPRequestHandler, ThreadingHTTPServer\\n\\nFAMILIES = {\\\"ACTIVITY\\\", \\\"WELLNESS\\\", \\\"CALENDAR\\\", \\\"CHATS\\\", \\\"LIBRARY\\\", \\\"SETTINGS\\\"}\\nSTATE = {\\\"unauthorized\\\": False}\\n\\n\\ndef valid_scopes(scope):\\n    seen = set()\\n    for tok in scope.split(\\\",\\\"):\\n        parts = tok.split(\\\":\\\")\\n        if len(parts) != 2 or parts[0] not in FAMILIES or parts[1] not in (\\\"READ\\\", \\\"WRITE\\\"):\\n            return False\\n        if parts[0] in seen:          # READ and WRITE for the same scope\\n            return False\\n        seen.add(parts[0])\\n    return bool(seen)\\n\\n\\nclass H(BaseHTTPRequestHandler):\\n    def log_message(self, *a):\\n        pass\\n\\n    def send_json(self, code, obj):\\n        body = json.dumps(obj).encode()\\n        self.send_response(code)\\n        self.send_header(\\\"Content-Type\\\", \\\"application/json\\\")\\n        self.send_header(\\\"Content-Length\\\", str(len(body)))\\n        self.end_headers()\\n        self.wfile.write(body)\\n\\n    def do_GET(self):\\n        url = urllib.parse.urlsplit(self.path)\\n        q = dict(urllib.parse.parse_qsl(url.query))\\n        if url.path == \\\"/oauth/authorize\\\":\\n            scope = q.get(\\\"scope\\\", \\\"\\\")\\n            if not q.get(\\\"client_id\\\") or not q.get(\\\"redirect_uri\\\") or not valid_scopes(scope):\\n                return self.send_json(400, {\\\"error\\\": \\\"invalid_request\\\"})\\n            back = q[\\\"redirect_uri\\\"] + \\\"?\\\" + urllib.parse.urlencode(\\n                {\\\"code\\\": \\\"mock-code-1234\\\", \\\"state\\\": q.get(\\\"state\\\", \\\"\\\")})\\n            self.send_response(302)\\n            self.send_header(\\\"Location\\\", back)\\n            self.end_headers()\\n            return\\n        if url.path.startswith(\\\"/api/v1/athlete/\\\"):\\n            if STATE[\\\"unauthorized\\\"]:\\n                return self.send_json(401, {\\\"error\\\": \\\"invalid_token\\\"})\\n            return self.send_json(200, {\\\"id\\\": \\\"2026-11-08\\\", \\\"weight\\\": 70.1,\\n                                        \\\"resting_heart_rate\\\": 52})\\n        self.send_json(404, {\\\"error\\\": \\\"not found\\\"})\\n\\n    def do_POST(self):\\n        url = urllib.parse.urlsplit(self.path)\\n        if url.path == \\\"/api/oauth/token\\\":\\n            body = urllib.parse.parse_qsl(self.rfile.read(\\n                int(self.headers.get(\\\"Content-Length\\\", 0))).decode())\\n            f = dict(body)\\n            if not f.get(\\\"client_id\\\") or not f.get(\\\"client_secret\\\"):\\n                return self.send_json(400, {\\\"error\\\": \\\"invalid_client\\\"})\\n            if f.get(\\\"grant_type\\\") == \\\"refresh_token\\\":\\n                return self.send_json(400, {\\\"error\\\": \\\"invalid_grant\\\"})\\n            return self.send_json(200, {\\n                \\\"token_type\\\": \\\"Bearer\\\",\\n                \\\"access_token\\\": \\\"mock-access-token-9f3c1e\\\",\\n                \\\"scope\\\": f.get(\\\"scope_granted\\\", \\\"ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE\\\"),\\n                \\\"athlete\\\": {\\\"id\\\": \\\"i98765\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"T. Rivera\\\"}})\\n        self.send_json(404, {\\\"error\\\": \\\"not found\\\"})\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    STATE[\\\"unauthorized\\\"] = os.path.exists(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), \\\"401\\\"))\\n    ThreadingHTTPServer((\\\"127.0.0.1\\\", 8899), H).serve_forever()\\n\",\"path\":\".e2e/mock_intervals.py\"}"}}]}
